  "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{1}{2}+0 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{18} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =9 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =1\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $x=4$ and $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(-2,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
